---
import ChapterLayout from '../../../layouts/ChapterLayout.astro';
import { getDrakeChapter } from '../../../data/story/drakeChaptersData';
import { processDrakeContentHtml } from '../../../utils/drakeContentProcessor';

const chapter = getDrakeChapter('013-light', 'chapter-2')!;

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;

const rawContentHtml = "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Chapter 2, and now for another party!\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Onion_Powah.21\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Onion_Powah!\">Onion Powah!</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Onion Powah!\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_11?action=edit&amp;section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Onion Powah!\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>I like that D012 made the fairly simple alteration of putting the storylines in a sensical, somewhat chronological order, rather than just leave you to figure it out yourself. Anyway, character time.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>PLAYABLE CHARACTER - <b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Onion_Knight_(Dissidia)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Onion Knight (Dissidia)\">Onion Knight</a></b>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/56/Dissidia_OnionKnight.png/revision/latest?cb=20101219074028\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Dissidia OnionKnight\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/56/Dissidia_OnionKnight.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/175?cb=20101219074028\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"175\" height=\"268\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"Dissidia OnionKnight.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissidia_OnionKnight.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>The Onion Knight, much like the Warrior of Light, has the problem of being an original character. They made him more memorable though, he's a cheeky wimp who is actually quite cowardly and foolish, and puts up an act of being brave and intelligent to hide it. He's given a pretty weak character arc as a result, but even if his development isn't all that interesting, he's still amusing and memorable, in part to a good VA performance from Aaron Spaan.\n</p><p>The Onion Knight is a fast and agile character, armed with fast-hitting low-range sword attacks and slow long-range magic attacks. His attacks don't do much damage though, but he makes up for it with HP links. Uniquely, while other characters learn their HP links by mastering appropriate attacks, the Onion Knight learns BRV to BRV attacks, then once he masters the BRV link, he learns the HP link. This means mastery of his attacks costs less AP, though totalled with the BRV link it's about the same as other characters, and his attacks can all link to Bravery or HP attacks, like Blizzard to Blizzaga or Quake. This goes for all his Bravery attacks too. His HP attacks are slow to start but are similarly divided into sword and magic. He later learns \"booster\" abilities to give him temporary boosts to his attack, defense and critical hit rate for either magic or physical attacks. There's not much to talk about when it comes to what his attacks do, you start out with all four of them and what you see is what you get, they're pretty straightforward.\n</p><p>The Onion Knight's problem is that he's incredibly predictable, because aside from his link attacks, he has only 8 attacks, 4 Bravery, two in the air one each for melee and magic, two on the ground for melee and magic, and 4 HP attacks, same distribution. This means at most times he only has four attacks available to him, and three of them - the spell and HPs - are slow to start up while the melee one is easily blocked. This unfortunately makes the Onion Knight one of the weakest characters in the game. He's not one of my #4 that I never use, but he is certainly one of my last choices aside from them for a fight. Against the AI they're of course too stupid to realize his flaws, but I'll reckon human opponents are no threat. But if you're really good at faking out the opponent and playing mind games, I guess give him a shot. As I've said before though, this walkthrough is only concerned with story mode, not human opposition. In that regard the Onion Knight is perfectly capable, though still low on the ladder and outclassed by many other characters.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Time to equip the Onion Knight of course. He can't use the Mythril Helm stuff, so I gave him the Snowscepter, Wakizashi, Wizard's Har and Silken Shirt. I bought him three more accessory slots and gave him a Hyper Ring, Muscle Belt, HP = 100%, BRV ≥ Base Value, and Level 1 - 9. I'll be relying on his melee attacks in this story since they hit faster and do more damage. Also note I had an AP calendar bonus, helpful indeed since I'll automatically get 3 more AP per fight and will master Onion's attacks quicker.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Delusory Knight\"><img alt=\"Delusory Knight\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Iifa Leaf\"><img alt=\"Iifa Leaf\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><div style=\"overflow:hidden;float:left;margin:0 1px\"><div style=\"position:relative;left:-0px;margin-right:-30px;top:-10px;margin-bottom:-15px;;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d0/Dissicon_ff6_Ter1.png/revision/latest?cb=20101120015142\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Dissicon ff6 Ter1\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"64\" height=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissicon ff6 Ter1.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissicon_ff6_Ter1.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d0/Dissicon_ff6_Ter1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/64?cb=20101120015142\" /></a></span></div></div>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Booster Accessory x5\"><img alt=\"Booster Accessory x5\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Blue.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Blue.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"><img alt=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Counterfeit Youth\"><img alt=\"Counterfeit Youth\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"1990 gil\"><img alt=\"1990 gil\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Straight Chain on the blue emblem to get all four of them, we still have a KP Gambler from last time, hang onto it still. The KP Chance is a 60 second victory, easy to hit because the blue emblem tacks a 5x booster on top of your normal boosters, so my modest 2.9 becomes 14.6, times a 12% damage boost to physical attacks. Feel the pain, manikins. The accessory gimmick enemies like for this story are seven Near Loss boosters with a Hyper Ring. If you're nervous then use a super-powered blow to kill them in one hit.\n</p><p>Enter the opposition. The Ephemeral Summoner uses Aerospark, a ground charging attack, and Impulse, and uses two HP attacks, Energy Ray and Diamond Dust. She has an Assist, shockingly since the Hard enemies didn't, it's a Phantasmal Girl. Finally a Counterfeit Wraith, it has the ground lash and energy ball and the spinning tentacle aerial Bravery attacks, and the Long Range Particle Beam HP attack.\n</p><p>Next, the Delusory Knight has those accessories with the Chocobo summon, which randomizes the Bravery of both characters. For attacks he has Shadow Lance, Nightfall, a quick downward dive that explodes on impact, and the Dark Flame HP attack. Next is a Counterfeit Youth, Onion Knight's manikin, he uses his Bravery melee attacks with the Magic Pot summon. BTW, Onion Knight has Turbo Hit and Multi Hit for his attacks and they link to Extra Hit and Extra Slice. I hate when attack names don't help me remember - or describe - what they do, so I'll just say aerial combo and ground combo.\n</p><p>As you fight just get use to Onion's attacks. His spells are useless until he gets their follow-ups, but with my AP boost he had them by the end of this gateway, it might take you until the next one to get them, once he has them he can use the follow-ups to begin a Chase. Keep in mind the Muscle Belt only boosts physical damage, his spells will get the Hyper Ring's boost but that's it. Also note his Blade Torrent has surprising range both horizontally and vertically. When they're taken care of the chests have 1990 gil and an Iifa Leaf.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Pursuit\">The Pursuit</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Pursuit\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_11?action=edit&amp;section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Pursuit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Terra senses a strange presence, and the Knight is eager to check it out in case it's a Crystal. Terra is nervous for some reason though, but he assures her if they find something unpleasant, he can handle it. On the world map, look on the beach immediately behind you for a Rosetta Stone, then go ahead and to the right. Far to the left as you emerge is a chest with 1000 gil. At the ruined castle, shatter the stone and cross to the island for an Assist Charge. The Moogle has some useless summons for us, and also sells those five EX and Assist boosters. We want the Empty Assist Gauge booster, but I can't afford it at 100 KP, if you can take it, if not, we'll get it soon, don't worry. We have that KP Gambler waiting for a gateway with five enemies. Buy a Round Chain, if the four orbs of the dead here didn't give you one.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"False Hero\"><img alt=\"False Hero\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phantasmal Harlequin\"><img alt=\"Phantasmal Harlequin\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazy