data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d0/Dissicon_ff6_Ter1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/64?cb=20101120015142\" /></a></span></div></div>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Capricious Thief\"><img alt=\"Capricious Thief\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Initial BRV Boost\"><img alt=\"Initial BRV Boost\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Pretty simple, Round Chain at D3. You could also use a Multichain in a few laces to get the emblems active, but you'll only get 10 KP for chaining 3 and beating the four yourself, and Multichains cost 10 KP to replace, so it's just a waste of time. The bonus line is 3 and the KP chance is a 90 second win.\n</p><p>First enemy, a Phantasmal Harlequin with Scatter-Spray Blizzaga, no threat. Then a Fleeting Flash, she uses Launch, Smite, Aerora, has a False Hero (Warrior of Light) Assist, the Chocobo summon, and those Near Loss accessories. Not a threat, as a note though I just got lucky here and Battlegen'd a Mythril piece from her, maybe you got lucky with her or a previous foe? Well sorry, I'll cover this quickly when we're done. Then the Strange Battle Piece, the False Hero. He uses Shield Strike and Rising Buckler with the HP links for both, has a big Bravery boost, uses Carbuncle to sap your Bravery when he lands a hit, and has a Phantasmal Harlequin for an Assist. With it dead mop up the Capricious Thief, it has Scoop Art, Solituion 9, uses Shift Break for it's HP attack (so don't use Comet just in case), and has the Magic Pot summon, those accessories again, and an unknown Assist, he never attacked enough to charge up his gauge for me to see who it was.\n</p><p>As we leave the gateway, the two find Exdeath. The Onion Knight is promptly intimidated and decides to play weak, telling him that they're too weak to give him a proper fight. Exdeath knows it's an act but decides to let them go, warning the Knight that cowards will never find the Crystal. He leaves, and the Knight boasts he never fights opponents he doesn't know for sure he can beat. Terra thinks Exdeath came more to deliver that message than to fight, but the Knight is ticked and insists fighting a stronger foe isn't courage, it's reckless, and he'll prove he's not a coward by finding his Crystal. Exdeath meanwhile tells Kefka Terra is out of his grasp, but Kefka isn't listening.\n</p><p>Now as I said, I got a piece of Mythril and used it to buy a Mythril Hairpin, which with the Sword and Bangle give the Knight the three pieces he needs. I naturally switched to the Mythril items, if you weren't so lucky as me and you probably won't be since I'm surprised I got it myself, keep going as you are now.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"><img alt=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\"