 decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Counterfeit Youth\"><img alt=\"Counterfeit Youth\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phantasmal Girl\"><img alt=\"Phantasmal Girl\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Cloud of Darkness\"><img alt=\"Cloud of Darkness\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ghost Rag\"><img alt=\"Ghost Rag\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Cross Chain at C3 to get them all, use that KP Gambler now for a smooth 75 KP. The blue emblem is a Booster x5, so your 3.3x boost will jump to 16.5x. Feel the pain, manikins. The bonus line is 14, and the KP Chance is a 90 second win, easy when you have such a lovely booster buff and the enemies are no higher level than Hard. We have a boss at the end of course but no Potion, so build up your EX Gauge during these fights, of course make the KP Chance in time but use Chases and such to charge up. Feel free to take HP damage since you have Cure to heal before the boss.\n</p><p>First, a Counterfeit Youth, it has Blade Torrent for an HP attack and Onion Knight's melee Bravery attacks. Next, a False Stalwart. It has that Hyper Ring with the Near Loss boosters, uses the Carbuncle summonstone, and has Earthquake, once again just stay in the air and you'll be fine. Third is a Counterfeit Wraith, it uses two tentacle attacks, the spinning one on the ground and the spherical whipping one in the air, and Long Range Particle Beam for an HP attack. And of course it has those accessories, and the Magic Pot summon. Next is a Phantasmal Girl, she has those accessories too with Carbuncle, uses Blizzara, and has Tornado as an HP attack. Stay away from her when she's in the air, don't want to get hit by accident right? Finally, another Counterfeit Youth, armed with Blizzard, Thunder, and Firaga for his HP attack. Firaga is only dangerous if you're at the right range for it to arc and hit you, further or closer and no problem, if you are in the butter zone though it can explode large enough to hit you even in the air, so if you see it charge up Firaga, run away or dash towards him, depending on your distance, use your best judgement. You can use Firaga yourself in the lead-up fights if you want an idea of how far it fires and thus how to avoid it yourself.\n</p><p>This is of course due to my AP boosts from yesterday, but I got enough during this last round of enemies to learn Quake, branching from Blizzard. Not as good as Swordshower since it has no wall rush but it does have range since it branches from Blizzard, and a pretty funny animation. Onion Knight's attack animations involve a lot of wacky cartoon antics huh? The chest has a Ghost Rag for you, grab it, use Cure if needed, and approach the end piece. Onion Knight feigns submission to get between the Cloud of Darkness and Terra and declares that his policy of fighting opponents he can't beat hasn't changed - he's just decided that his head is wrong, because his heart tells him he can win. That makes no sense, but then a lot of the morals of the original Dissidia's stories were screwed up. Anyway, boss time, fortunately Terra vanishes from the arena as other characters tend to do.\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Cloud_of_Darkness_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Cloud of Darkness (Dissidia PSP)\">Cloud of Darkness</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/46/CoDDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110228054507\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"CoDDissidiaRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"137\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"CoDDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-image-key=\"CoDDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/46/CoDDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/137?cb=20110228054507\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">3,304\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">20\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">543\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Tentacle of Scorn, Tentacle of Pain, Tentacle of Spite, Tentacle of Suffering\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Wide-Angle Particle Beam, Anti-Air Particle Beam, Aura Ball, Fusillade Particle Beam, 0-Form Particle Beam\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Hecatoncheir\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">2/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The Cloud of Darkness has the same moveset as when we faced her with Laguna way back in Chapter 3 of the 012 story, but this time she has a level advantage on us and four Blue Gems, each of them giving her another 60 base Bravery. That 543 Bravery in the table is her base Bravery <i>before</i> factoring in the boost she gets from being at a higher level. In short, she can rapidly knock off large chunks of your HP with little effort, so knowing her HP attacks and how to avoid them is crucial. Fortunately you've faced her and the manikins of her a lot by this point so you know how to do so. That same Bravery also makes it harder to Break her, and of course when you finally do there's Hecatoncheir to rain on the parade.\n</p><p>0-Form Particle Beam is the worst threat, its range outstrips that of the Onion Knight's attacks, its damage priority will deflect or cancel out all his attacks, and at close-range it's hard to dodge and inflicts wall rush. Feel like eating 900 points of HP damage from one hit? Because it's probably going to happen if she fires off 0-Form while you're close enough for her to hit you with it. Unless you can hit her as she begins the attack, find a quickmove icon and run away quickly. Ultimately though all her attacks are dangerous due to the sheer versatility of them and her high Bravery. She's not as stupid as you might have come to expect from the AI at this point, she one blocked my attack and fires off a 0-Form right in my face. Not pleasant.\n</p><p>Your safest bet is to land a blow as she tries a tentacle attack, block it and hit her as she staggers, remember your HP links if you've learned any. Onion Knight's HP attacks are slow so she's very liable to damage you as you recover if she avoids you. She's ultimately not too bad because she still isn't <i>that</i> smart, just smarter than a lot of previous enemies. She gets a 2 on my template solely for her high Bravery letting you blast you into the Void with only a few hits. Otherwise, not much harder than any previous boss.\n</p><p>With her defeated she fades into darkness, and Golbez arrives to speak to us again. Onion Knight vows to protect Terra from him, and for following his heart and proving himself his Crystal manifests for him. Terra awakens, though still weak, and fall unconscious again shortly after. The Onion Knight, tired after his battle, follows suit. However the danger isn't over, because with the Cloud of Darkness's failure, Kefka is ready to take the stage and finish what she couldn't.\n</p><p>We also unlock a Report with fights in it, to the Report section, kiddies!\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 10\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 4\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 6\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Light to All\">Light to All</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/013-light/prologue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 9\">Prologue</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 10\">Chapter 1</a> - <strong class=\"mw-se